## QA escalation response — C5 is now RESOLVED, not adjudicated away

QA ruled v3's C5 (cracked sub-band hi-freq ~7.1 vs 8–9) a **genuine FAIL**. I did not weaken the
threshold. Two things were done:

1. **Measurement corrected.** The v3 report's 7.12 was measured on the **512² render**, while the
   donor anchor (8.42) was measured on a **200² bilinear downsample** — not apples-to-apples. The
   mini-baker now contains `patch_interior_hifreq()` which downsamples BOTH render and patch mask
   to 200², selects fully covered interior pixels (mask>220) and computes `|L − Blur5(L)|`. With the
   v3 settings this corrected measurement is **9.21** (above the band, not below).
2. **Construction tuned (A8).** Patch opacity 0.85 → 0.80 (spec JSON untouched) brings the rendered
   cracked grain to **8.66**, inside the donor 8–9 band, while dark coverage stays 10.97% (≤25%).
   This is a real recipe change, verified by the corrected donor-convention measurement.

Fresh donor measurements supporting the band (probe `t6_t15_c5_probe.py`, temp only):

