I re-read the shipped `t6_desert_variant_compare.png` after the v4 render. Against the donor
reference panel: the port is donor-family olive-khaki sand (L 105.6) versus the reference's warm
orange-tan wooden siding — the port is **not** a colour match, deliberately, because the reference is
LOW confidence, visually not ground, and C1 rejects L≥128 dominance. The piece shows irregular
clustered cracked/scree patches with hairline cracks and empty ground between them (no repeated
stamps), and a dry gray boulder with a soft contact shadow sitting on the ground (no hard-edged
floating rock). R>G>B everywhere; no green cast. **Honest verdict: PASS on all defects the
coordinator reported; still cooler/darker and less polygonal than donor `desert2/3` facets** — a
known remaining stylistic gap, not a criterion failure.

